# .mutation-allowlist - surviving (LIVED) mutants accepted as already known.
#
# SCOPE: this allowlist covers ONLY the packages inside the mutation gate scope
# (see MUTATE_EXCLUDE in the Makefile): internal/config and internal/store.
# Mutations outside that scope are not run at all, so they can never appear here.
#
# Format:  <MUTATOR> <file>:<line>
#
# Add an entry ONLY when the mutant is provably equivalent (no test can ever kill
# it, because the mutation does not change observable behaviour) or the gap is a
# conscious, accepted risk. Adding a real test gap here hides a real risk, and
# mutation testing exists precisely to surface those.
#
# Seeded from a full-module `go tool gremlins unleash` run. Entries are keyed by
# LINE NUMBER, so inserting code above an entry shifts it and will surface a new
# red on purpose: re-verify the gap and update this file, do not regenerate it
# wholesale (that would silently re-hide real gaps).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every entry below is a PROVABLY EQUIVALENT MUTANT: the replacement is
# observationally identical to the original for every possible input, so no test
# can kill it. Each one states why. Do not add real test gaps here.
#
# Negated guards deserve extra care: CONDITIONALS_NEGATION flips WHICH BRANCH
# RUNS, so "equivalent" means the newly-taken branch is a proven no-op, not that
# the removed branch was the last statement. query_history.go:193 was briefly
# parked here on exactly that mistake; the mutant swallowed a failed rename.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# keybindings_groups.go:123 - `if n < lo` -> `if n <= lo` (digitRange min).
# The mutation only fires when n == lo, and the body is `lo = n`, which is a
# no-op at equality. Same input, same lo, forever.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/config/keybindings_groups.go:123

# keybindings_groups.go:126 - `if n > hi` -> `if n >= hi` (digitRange max).
# Mirror of the entry above: fires only at n == hi, where `hi = n` is a no-op.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/config/keybindings_groups.go:126

# scanner.go:47 - `projects[i].Path < projects[j].Path` -> `<=`, inside the
# `projects[i].Path != projects[j].Path` guard. `a < b` and `a <= b` can only
# differ when a == b, but the guard already sent equal paths to the Name
# comparison. Both operands are therefore always distinct here.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/config/scanner.go:47

# scanner.go:214 - `a.project.Path < b.project.Path` -> `<=`, the lexicographic
# tiebreak after the equal-length guard. Only equal strings could distinguish
# them, and isBetterSurvivor is never called with the same candidate twice;
# two candidates in a group that shared a path would be the same FoundProject,
# so the winner is unobservable either way.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/config/scanner.go:214

# query_history.go:76 - `len(s.entries) > 500` -> `>= 500` (history cap).
# At exactly 500 entries the mutant slices entries[0:], which is the same 500
# entries the original keeps. The cap is only observable above 500, where both
# versions take the last 500.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/store/query_history.go:76

# query_history.go:87 - `i < j` -> `i <= j` in the All() reversal loop.
# The extra iteration only runs once the pointers meet, and it swaps the middle
# element with itself. Reversal is unchanged for even and odd lengths alike.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/store/query_history.go:87

# query_history.go:101 - `i < j` -> `i <= j` in the Favorites() reversal loop.
# Same self-swap of the middle element as the All() loop above.
CONDITIONALS_BOUNDARY internal/store/query_history.go:101
